# Supabase — the real backend (see the handoff notes, section 10).
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values from
# Supabase → Project Settings → API. .env.local is gitignored; this template
# is not, so the two variable names are always documented in the repo.
#
# With neither variable set the app runs on the seeded demo fleet in
# localStorage, which is what a fresh clone does.
#
# Both values below are visible in the browser bundle by design — row-level
# security is what protects the data, not the key. Never put the service_role
# key in a VITE_* variable: it bypasses row-level security entirely.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
